#====================================================================
# DRAFT - OHOS distributed fs denies file-create in mktemp 0700 dirs
#   and O_APPEND opens for the conan task; breaks every autotools
#   config.status run on affected devices
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-hmdfs-mktemp-0700-append-deny
trigger_tool:           autoconf|configure|config.status|mktemp
phase:                  configuration
error_signature: >-
  can't create .*/subs1\.awk: Permission denied|
  \.deps/.*Permission denied|
  bad interpreter: Permission denied

severity:               2
category:               fs|ohos|autotools|portability|hmdfs
match_keywords:         mktemp -d, 0700, Permission denied, O_APPEND, append,
                        subs1.awk, config.status, distributed fs, HMDFS,
                        hmmac=use_task, task label
title:                  OHOS distributed fs denies file-create inside mktemp 0700 dirs and O_APPEND opens for conan-task processes

root_cause:             On the /storage/Users distributed fs (hmmac=use_task), directories created by `mktemp -d` get mode 0700 with an ACL fixed at creation; on affected devices even the owning task cannot create files inside them, and `chmod 777` does not rebuild the ACL. Separately, opens with O_APPEND (`cat >> file`, `echo >> file`) are denied for the conan process tree on affected devices while the same operations succeed from an interactive SSH session. Autoconf 2.71 config.status hardcodes its temp dir in the cwd and assembles subs1.awk via `cat >>`, so every autotools configure fails at "could not setup config files machinery" on such devices.
affected_scope: >-
  Every autotools package configured inside a conan-home on the distributed fs
  of an affected device (policy varies per device: one device completed
  config.status normally, another denied it consistently). Compiled objects
  that reference g_libintl_* also need a link stub because OHOS ships no
  libintl.
verification_cmd:       d=$(mktemp -d /storage/Users/currentUser/x/confXXXXXX) && echo t > "$d/f" && echo OK || echo DENIED; echo a > f && echo b >> f && cat f; stat -f /storage/Users/currentUser | grep -E "Type|Inodes"

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           pre-created-fixed-tmpdir-plus-recipe-patch
rec_description:        Pre-create the config.status temp dir with plain `mkdir -p` plus `chmod 777` (a plain-mkdir dir behaves correctly; a chmod-fixed mktemp dir does not), then patch configure/config.status to use it via ${TMPDIR:-.}/cs instead of mktemp. Sign any freshly built executable with binary-sign-tool before a make rule invokes it. For gettext references (g_libintl_gettext et al.) link a passthrough stub archive (E508). Retry only after the distributed fs client state has settled; deletion storms from concurrent cleanups poison the same subtrees.
rec_command:            mkdir -p "${TMPDIR:-.}/cs" && chmod 777 "${TMPDIR:-.}/cs"; sed -i 's|.*mktemp -d.*|tmp="${TMPDIR:-.}/cs" \&\& mkdir -p "$tmp" \&\& chmod 777 "$tmp" \&\&|' config.status; sh ./config.status && make -j1
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe-patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      run-on-device-without-fs-deny-policy
fallback_description:   Devices differ in this policy (one device completed config.status normally, another denied it consistently). Provisioning should unify the policy; otherwise pick a device of the permissive class for autotools packages.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          device-selection

forbid_1_pattern:       chmod 777.*confXXXXXX.*fixed
forbid_1_reason:        chmod does not rebuild the ACL baked into a 0700 mktemp dir; claiming it as a fix wastes build rounds.
forbid_1_consequence:   The same create denial recurs and the diagnosis is polluted.

forbid_2_pattern:       concurrent heavy fs tasks during configure diagnosis
forbid_2_reason:        Concurrent long tasks (e.g. full Qt builds) on the shared distributed fs produce intermittent ENOENT/EACCES/Errno 28 that mimic and mask the real cause.
forbid_2_consequence:   Root cause misattributed; rounds wasted on symptoms.

principles:             P016
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E316]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

